name    mod-dungeon-challenge: the NPC's dungeon lists page instead of passing the gossip limit
# Server-side test bot run (mod-fl-testbots), T1. A gossip menu holds at most 32 options and the core ASSERTs past
# that (a worldserver crash). The Dungeon Challenge NPC (500000) listed every enabled dungeon in one menu: 25 today,
# 35 once the 10 delves are added. The lists now show 20 dungeons per page with "Next page >>" / "<< Previous page".
# Dungeons are listed by map id; the last one today, FL: Yelma (748), is on page 2, Utgarde Keep (574) on page 1.
timeout 120s

bot a warrior
group party

place 727 13288.5 11776.2 -31.5
require a alive
pick stone creature:500000 near a
require stone exists
do a approach stone

log 1 - the start list: page 1 holds 20 dungeons and a next-page option
do a gossip stone
expect output has "Start Dungeon Challenge"
do a select 0
expect output has "Utgarde Keep"
expect output has "Next page >>"
expect output lacks "FL: Yelma"
expect output lacks "option 23:"

log 2 - page 2 holds the rest and a previous-page option
do a select 20
expect output has "FL: Yelma"
expect output has "<< Previous page"
expect output lacks "Utgarde Keep"

log 3 - a dungeon on page 2 opens its difficulty menu
do a select 0
expect output has "Level 1"

log 4 - the leaderboard and records lists page the same way
do a gossip stone
do a select 1
expect output has "Next page >>"
expect output lacks "FL: Yelma"
do a select 20
expect output has "FL: Yelma"
do a gossip stone
do a select 3
expect output has "Next page >>"
do a select 20
expect output has "FL: Yelma"

cleanup
place 727 13288.5 11776.2 -31.5
